      with init_image/mem_setup/segments/auth_and_reset, ready/fatal/handover on SMP2P, GLINK descriptor and FIFOs, the client queue).
      Changed: SM8750 addresses (IPCC 0x406000, RSC drv-2 0x16520000, carveouts 0xb8200000 + 0x5780000 and 0x9ed80000 + 0x80000);
      no interrupts (the IPCC doorbells and the RSC completion are polled from the DSP thread: the native KC has no
      armcpu_spi_attach); the secure calls through Sm8750Scm instead of its own SMC loop; one firmware source (modem_a, or
      piano-power-fw=DIR); numbered steps with a console line before and after each, every secure call and RSC/IPCC register write
      traced, piano-power-delay/stop/qmp/rpmh/trace; a status struct instead of the native_adsp_stats arrays; the survey exported for
      piano-power=1. The lcx/lmx vote is written fresh (vote() in PianoAdsp.cpp) after Linux rpmh-rsc's request sequence (idle TCS
      by DRV_STATUS, trigger and mode cleared in that order, CMD_STATUS checked, a TCS in flight left alone); sheng's
      qcom_rpmh_active_request/qcom_rpmh_finish are no longer called (QcomRpmh.c still provides the cmd-db lookup and the layout).
      The segments are stored with aligned 8-byte stores (no memcpy/bzero) into a mapping limited to the image's span, after a
      read/write-back probe of the carveout; piano-power-map and piano-power-load-first choose the mapping type and the order. The
      rail votes hold PianoA830's DRV-2 owner word (sm8750_rpmh_drv2_owner, its documented protocol: compare-exchange 0 for our
      tag, 10 us between tries, at most 2 s), imported by name because PianoA830 links before PianoPower. Every secure call and
      each image's PAS sequence also hold PianoA830's secure-call lock word (sm8750_scm_owner, package/include/PianoScmLock.h,
      docs/scm-lock.md), imported the same way.
