Specification only (GPL-2.0, read, never copied): the piano MCA property protocol, its property ids and the stock policy values,
from Project-SunUEFI patches/linux/7.3/0001-platform.patch (drivers/power/supply/piano_mca.c, GPL-2.0-only) and its
docs/devel/linux/kernel.md; Ubuntu's piano-charging.service (xiaomipad-8pro-mainline packaging) and the shipped xiaomi_mca.ko module
descriptions. PianoMca.c describes and implements that behaviour in its own code. The bq27z561 standard commands come from TI's
datasheet; the SM8750 addresses from piano's live DT (out/inputs/piano-boot.dtb). The K90 annibale drivers
(unixnu-research/hackios-xnu-kernel-k90, annibale_adsp.c and annibale_adsp_fw.inc, APSL-2.0) were read for facts only (that the
SM8750 DSP starts from XNU at EL1; its order, TCS choice and the no-overlapping-secure-calls rule; the charger property family it
names, docs/drivers/charging.md §5a and §5c); no code is taken.

Xiaomi's stock charger modules (the mca_*, qcom_subpmic_proxy and qcom_adsp_pd_protocol binaries in the stock vendor_boot ramdisk)
are proprietary and are NOT a source for this package: no property id, register map or sequence here comes from disassembling them.
The ids come from the GPL driver's text and the APSL K90 port's notes, read as descriptions, and are confirmed on the device. Not used at all: Linux's qcom_battmgr, qcom_q6v5_pas, bq27xxx and spmi-pmic-arb sources.

Specification only (GPL-2.0, read for wire facts, never copied), 2026-11-11: the Ubuntu piano kernel (unixnu-research/ubuntu-ref/kernel,
branch piano/dev) as digested in docs/ubuntu-history/device.md and kernel.md: the board configuration (0x201c, 0x201a, 0x201b and their
values and order), the charger_pd gate and the per-generation re-send, the diag property ids, the PAN and UCSI message layouts
(pmic_glink_altmode.c, ucsi_glink.c: the 24-byte PAN write, the header-only UCSI buffer read answered by the buffer and a return code)
and the service registry messages (Linux's PDR message definitions: listener registration 0x20, state indication 0x22, ack 0x23 and
their TLV ids). Servreg.h, the listener in PianoQrtr.c and the PianoMca.c additions are written fresh from those descriptions; the
UCSI buffer offsets (VERSION 0, CCI 4) are the UCSI specification's. The Type-C sink status's Rp bit order in ChargerPmic.h (bit 3
default, bit 2 1.5 A, bit 1 3.0 A) is the register fact of Linux's drivers/usb/typec/tcpm/qcom/qcom_pmic_typec_port.c (GPL, read for
the fact only; docs/drivers/usb-host.md §facts).

