docs/drivers/thermal.md §12.7, the precedence of a sink's sources of current (PD, Type-C current, BC 1.2, default USB power) from
the USB Type-C specification. Nothing copied.

ChargerWdog.h (the charger watchdog, 2026-11-12, docs/drivers/charging-policy.md §18) is new code (BSD-2-Clause-Patent). Register facts
only, read and never copied (GPL-2.0): the Ubuntu piano kernel tree (unixnu-research/ubuntu-ref/kernel, Linux 7.2.15)
drivers/power/supply/qcom_smbx.c (sha256 228d32a70853a7488bc299f9ddb9e34f1d942c7834d9ec049ad3d8fc76efed3c; PMI8998): the MISC
watchdog registers (+0x43 pet bit 0, +0x51 WD_CFG and its bits, +0x53 with bit 7 "a bite disables charging" and the bark/bite fields),
MISC at the charger base + 0x600, the CHGR status 1 state field and its values, the charging enable command +0x42 and CHGR_CFG2 +0x51,
and that the host driver disables the watchdog's charging stop; arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/pm8150b.dtsi (sha256
bbca66e6618c1f6003c80753273059c17ba15be425787fece9a73b1e6108ab3a): the vbus regulator at the charger + 0x100 and Type-C at + 0x500.
Their places on PMIH010x are this repository's inference from its own logs. The owner-channel write in PianoPower.cpp is the arbiter
v7 write PianoDwc3 (setRestartReason) and PianoTorch (TorchCore.h) already make, re-expressed.

ChargerEnable.h (the charging enable command, 2026-11-12, docs/drivers/charging-policy.md §19) is new code (BSD-2-Clause-Patent).
Register facts only, from the same qcom_smbx.c (same sha256), read and never copied: CHGR +0x42 bit 0 the charging enable command;
CHGR_CFG2 +0x51 bit 7 CHG_EN_SRC (0 the command register, 1 the pin), bit 6 the pin's polarity, bits 5..0 (pre-to-fast, BAT_OV ECC,
I_TERM, AUTO_RECHG, analog drop, CHARGER_INHIBIT) and the host driver's value for it (software control, active high, inhibit on);
the pulse of piano-power-chgen=2 is this repository's experiment (that an edge of the command restarts this charger is a hypothesis,
not a fact of that source).
The arbiter's duplicate APID mappings of one PPID (one per EE) are what this repository's dev14 log shows.
